<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview">
    <div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
      <div class="page-hero__copy reveal">
        <span class="ey">Security review</span>
        <h1>Start with the buyer's actual security questions.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Public materials do not verify certifications, compliance programs or detailed infrastructure controls. Request the documentation that applies to your buyer and contract review.</p>
        <div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/contact/">Request security details &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#scope">Review product scope &darr;</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual reveal" aria-label="Security review scope"><div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Review scope</span><b>Verify</b></div><div class="visual-flow"><div class="visual-step is-accent"><i>01</i><span><strong>Data flow</strong><small>Buyer, store and documents</small></span><em>Map</em></div><div class="visual-step is-lavender"><i>02</i><span><strong>Access</strong><small>Connection and catalog scope</small></span><em>Confirm</em></div><div class="visual-step is-peach"><i>03</i><span><strong>Controls</strong><small>Current vendor materials</small></span><em>Request</em></div></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="scope"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Verified product scope</span><h2>Understand what the platform connects before reviewing controls.</h2><p class="lead">These are product workflow facts, not certifications or a substitute for the buyer's security review.</p></div><div class="feature-grid">
    <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">01</span><h3>Procurement to commerce</h3><p>PunchOut Central connects enterprise procurement workflows to Shopify or Shopify Plus supplier stores using cXML and OCI.</p><p><a href="/integrations/">Review integrations &rarr;</a></p></article>
    <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">02</span><h3>Buyer-specific catalog access</h3><p>Buyer connections can be associated with the relevant store and collections or catalog access.</p><p><a href="/platform/punchout/">Review catalog connectivity &rarr;</a></p></article>
    <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">03</span><h3>Transaction records</h3><p>The product describes visibility into sessions, carts, approvals, POs, store orders, invoices, line items, timestamps and activity.</p><p><a href="/platform/transactions/">Review transaction visibility &rarr;</a></p></article>
    <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">04</span><h3>Operational support</h3><p>Product materials describe in-product tickets, help or chat, FAQs and phone support. Confirm the current support terms for your agreement.</p><p><a href="/contact/">Contact the team &rarr;</a></p></article>
  </div></div></section>

  <section class="sec soft" id="questions"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Questions to request</span><h2>Ask for buyer-relevant evidence.</h2><p class="lead">The right review packet depends on the buyer, data flow and contract. Ask the team for the relevant answers rather than assuming a standard certification or control set.</p></div><div class="simple-steps">
    <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">01</span><h3>Data flow</h3><p>Ask what buyer, catalog, order and invoice information is exchanged and where each step is recorded.</p></article>
    <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">02</span><h3>Access model</h3><p>Confirm how buyer connections, store selection and catalog access are configured and reviewed.</p></article>
    <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">03</span><h3>Vendor materials</h3><p>Request architecture, subprocessors, retention, incident response and security documentation if required.</p></article>
    <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">04</span><h3>Contract terms</h3><p>Ask for the applicable service terms, privacy terms and support commitments before approval.</p></article>
  </div></div></section>

  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">No unsupported claims</span><h2>Bring the security questionnaire you actually need answered.</h2><p class="lead">PunchOut Central can review the buyer's requirements and provide the relevant materials for evaluation.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/contact/">Start a security review &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/documentation/">See documentation</a></div></div></section>
</main>
